# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Line endings are consensus-relevant in this repository.
#
# solc hashes the bytes of every source file into the contract metadata and
# appends that metadata's hash to the creation code. A checkout that turns LF
# into CRLF therefore changes the hash of every .sol file, which changes the
# metadata, which changes the creation code, which changes the CREATE2 address
# the frontend mines for the hook — so a launch from that build reverts with
# `InvalidHookSalt`, and Blockscout verification fails against the deployed
# bytecode.
#
# `core.autocrlf=true` is the Git for Windows default, and this repository was
# one `git clone` on a Windows machine away from exactly that. It has not
# happened only because the working tree here was written LF by an editor
# rather than materialised by a checkout. That is luck, not a property.
#
# See also foundry.toml, where the remappings are pinned for the same reason:
# both are inputs to the metadata hash that look like formatting.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

*               text=auto eol=lf

# Windows shells parse these by line and require CRLF.
*.bat           text eol=crlf
*.cmd           text eol=crlf

# Never touch these; conversion corrupts them.
*.png           binary
*.jpg           binary
*.jpeg          binary
*.gif           binary
*.ico           binary
*.webp          binary
*.woff          binary
*.woff2         binary
*.ttf           binary
*.otf           binary
*.pdf           binary
*.zip           binary
*.gz            binary
